	<!--
	  PALSAR-3 layout from here on: JAXA FTR-240031A Rev. A (2024-09-24), Table 4.6-5
	  "Data Set Summary Record", fields 100-155. Positions in the comments are the spec's,
	  1-based; the parser works 0-based. Everything above this comment is the stock 14.0.0
	  file unchanged and agrees with the same table.

	  Why the stock file is wrong from here: PALSAR-3 stores each Doppler block (along- and
	  cross-track centroid, along- and cross-track rate) as FOUR 3xF16.7 groups, one per
	  ScanSAR scan, where PALSAR-2 stores one. Each block grows by 144 bytes, and every field
	  after it lands in the wrong place: range_spacing and azimuth_spacing read 0, PASS reads
	  ASCENDING on a descending scene, the incidence polynomial reads 0.  Measured with
	  microwave-toolbox 14.0.0 on a real delivery, 2026-09-22.

	  Scans 2-4 are skipped: stripmap and spotlight fill scan 1 only, and SNAP reads scan 1.
	-->
	<rec name="Along track Doppler frequency centroid constant term" type="5" num="16"/>	<!-- #100  1415 -->
	<rec name="Along track Doppler frequency centroid linear term" type="5" num="16"/>
	<rec name="Along track Doppler frequency centroid quadratic term" type="5" num="16"/>
	<rec name="skipBytes" type="0" num="144"/>	<!-- #101-103 along-track centroid, scans 2-4  1463 -->
